      "description": "Head Coach, Varsity Blues Track & Field and Cross Country Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Head Coach, Varsity Blues Track & Field and Cross Country Date Posted: 09/01/2026 Req ID: 49785 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physl Ed. Department: Faculty of Kinesiology & Physl Ed Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The University of Toronto’s Faculty of Kinesiology and Physical Education is globally recognized for developing and advancing knowledge about the interactions of physical activity and health through outstanding undergraduate and graduate education programs, cutting-edge research and the delivery of sport, recreation and high performance athletic opportunities for students, staff, faculty and community members across the three campuses. In achieving this vision, the Faculty is guided by values of integrity, respect, equity and diversity. kpe.utoronto.ca. Your Opportunity: Reporting to the Director, Interuniversity and High Performance Athletics, the incumbent is responsible for overseeing the University’s track & field and cross country operations within established University guidelines, policies and procedures. Responsibilities include but are not limited to student athlete recruitment, track and field program athlete management, human resources and financial management, sport development, student athlete development, alumni relations, community development, ensuring safe sport compliance and acting as a technical resource. The incumbent is responsible for the design and implementation of a comprehensive sport development plan that is conducive to positioning U of T at a competitive level to achieve provincial and national prominence. The plan shall include financial and support services, annual and quadrennial performance targets, budget and revenue/expense tracking framework, team revenue generation targets, and evaluation framework to measure performance against agreed upon targets. The incumbent will be responsible for managing the finances of the track and field program, including both the operational budget and a restricted spending plan. Fundraising is a key component to the success of the program, and the incumbent is responsible for raising a minimum of 10% of the total of the two budgets annually. The incumbent is responsible for managing the recruitment processes for the interuniversity track & field and cross country program and maintaining the recruiting database. The head coach’s professional presentation of the benefits of attending the University of Toronto and being a member of the Varsity Blues is critical to the success of the program and our ability to attract excellent students and athletes to U of T. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: EDUCATION: University degree preferably in kinesiology/physical education or combination of equivalent experience. Fully certified National Performance Coach or High-Performance Coach level preferred, equivalency considered. EXPERIENCE: A minimum of 5 years coaching experience in OUA or U SPORTS and at least 3 years of head coaching experience or equivalent level of program experience. SKILLS: Demonstrated strong leadership, coaching and motivational skills. Teamwork and team building are essential to this role and the ability to collaborate within a collegial environment is paramount. Strong negotiation, and analytical skills required in relation to athlete issues and financial issues. Must have full technical knowledge of and be current in all the rules and regulation that govern World Athletics. Have a demonstrated ability to analyze all aspects of track & field and cross country. Must be knowledgeable in the OUA and USPORTS rules that govern the sport programs around recruiting, athletic scholarship, eligibility compliance rules. Basic Microsoft Suite (i.e. PowerPoint, Excel, Outlook). Experience working with relevant recruitment databases Good numeracy and record keeping skills OTHER: Sensitivity to and understanding of equity, diversity and inclusion and demonstrated skill to act on issues/problems/initiatives involving equity and diversity matters. Excellent interpersonal and oral communication skills; instructional, coaching and motivating skills. Demonstrated skills/abilities in planning and organizing, taking initiative, problem solving and exercising good judgment. Ability to maintain tact and composure in a highly competitive environment. Must be able to deal with crisis management related issues and manage public relations interactions with media, alumni and University officials. Closing Date: 09/30/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 4 -- Hiring Zone: $106,705 - $124,491 -- Broadband Salary Range: $106,705 - $177,843 Job Category: Athletics Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: PR, Academic, Fundraising, Database, Training, Marketing, Nonprofit, Education, Technology Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
