    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Front-Line-Service-Coordinator-ON/606082717/": {
      "title": "Front Line Service Coordinator",
      "description": "Front Line Service Coordinator Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Front Line Service Coordinator Date Posted: 09/14/2026 Req ID: 50165 Faculty/Division: School of Graduate Studies Department: School of Graduate Studies Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00039060 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About Us The School of Graduate Studies (SGS) promotes University-wide inclusive excellence in graduate education, research and professional training to ensure high standards across the various academic divisions, as well as supporting postdoctoral fellows. SGS defines and administers University-wide regulations for graduate education. We share responsibility for graduate education with graduate units and divisions, and operate through a system of collegial governance, consultation, and decanal leadership. SGS also provides expertise and advice; reviews the design and delivery of programs; develops performance standards; supports access, equitable inclusion, fairness, and ethical conduct in graduate education; organizes services and financial assistance to graduate students; encourages a close and positive relationship between research and graduate instruction and represents the cause of graduate education at the University of Toronto and in the broader academic and general community. More information about the School of Graduate Studies is at: http://www.sgs.utoronto.ca/Pages/default.aspx Your Opportunity: The Front Line Service Coordinator is the first point of contact for graduate students and administrators reaching out to the School of Graduate Studies. The incumbent responds to a high volume of enquiries, provides detailed information on processes, policies, and procedures, and directs students to the appropriate resources when a question falls outside the scope of the role. As the public face of the office, the incumbent brings professionalism and courtesy to every interaction, resolving routine issues and escalating more complex matters as required. Reporting to the Associate Director, Graduate Academic Services, the incumbent develops and coordinates the front-line schedule among all staff who provide front-line coverage and provides training and coaching for new procedures and staff. The Front-Line Service Coordinator updates and maintains student records in ROSI and GradApp (Slate),  ensuring information accuracy, currency, and consistency.  Sound judgment, attention to detail, and the ability to manage competing priorities in a fast-paced environment are essential to success in this role. Essential Qualifications: •    Bachelor's Degree or an acceptable combination of equivalent experience •    Minimum three (3) years of related experience in academic service delivery related to graduate education •    Experience working directly with the public in a front-line, customer service, or administrative role •    Experience updating and maintaining records in a student information system (e.g. ROSI, GradApp) or related database •    Strong verbal and written communication skills •    Strong attention to detail and accuracy in data entry •    Good time management and organizational skills, with the ability to manage a high volume of work and competing deadlines •    Resourceful, practical problem-solver, able to connect students with the right people and offices across the University, and to escalate and collaborate with other teams as needed •    Ability to remain professional and courteous, including in difficult or high-pressure interactions •    Proficiency with M365 Suite, including Outlook, Excel, Word, PowerPoint, and SharePoint •    Ability to work with minimal supervision Assets: •    Experience in graduate education at  the University of Toronto •    Experience with University of Toronto student information systems such as ROSI, GradApp (Slate), and customer relationship management systems Closing Date: 09/23/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 10 --  $72,119. with an annual step progression to a maximum of  $92,226. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Recruiter: Blythe Campbell Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: CRM, Data Entry, Information Systems, Relationship Manager, Equity, Technology, Administrative, Customer Service, Finance Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Events-&-Outreach-Officer-ON/606075917/": {
      "title": "Events & Outreach Officer Job Details",
      "description": "Events & Outreach Officer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Events & Outreach Officer Date Posted: 09/14/2026 Req ID: 50166 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Canadian Hub for Health Intelligence & Innovation in Infectious Diseases (HI3) Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00060047 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your opportunity: This position will support strategic activities of the University of Toronto’s Canadian Hub for Health Intelligence & Innovation in Infectious Diseases (HI3) and Emerging Pathogens & Infectious Diseases Consortium (EPIC). HI3 is a federally funded research and collaboration hub with over 100 academic, not-for-profit, and private sector members with the mandate to coordinate health emergency readiness and response. Bridging the University’s various divisions and hospital partners, EPIC is a collaborative institutional strategic initiative that marshals Toronto’s advanced research infrastructure and collective world-renowned research and training expertise to enable an integrated, innovative response to infectious diseases. Together, HI3 and EPIC contribute to preparing for future health emergencies, strengthening systems to advance resilience, and fostering innovations to help prevent the next pandemic. As the Events & Outreach Officer, reporting through HI3, you will support both HI3 and EPIC in the planning and delivery of strategic research events, symposia, workshops and outreach initiatives. Working across a network of academic, healthcare and other external partners, you will coordinate complex event activities and communications that support ecosystem engagement and the delivery of key program priorities. Your work will contribute to bringing partners together around infectious disease research, innovation and health emergency readiness. Your responsibilities will include: Conceptualizing, organizingand executing events and programming, including coordinating logistics and liaising with clients, vendors and service providers Conducting post-event evaluation and analysis and recommending changes to event planning activities Coordinating the drafting, production and dissemination of advertising, promotional and outreach materials Coordinating meeting schedules, agendas, materials, action and follow-up items Updating and maintaining event and program records, including ticketing databases Supporting event-related financial administration, including cost estimates and expense reimbursements Essential Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree or an acceptable combination of education and experience Minimum three (3) years of event coordination and outreach experience in a university environment Demonstrated experience conceptualizing, organizing and executing research events and programming, including symposia and workshops Demonstrated experience coordinating complex event logistics, including domestic and international travel, itineraries and accommodations for speakers and participants Experience supporting communications and outreach activities, including developing promotional and event materials and maintaining web content in WordPress Experience liaising with internal and external service providers and stakeholders Experience collecting and analyzing survey and event feedback and conducting post-event evaluations using REDCap and MS Forms Experience coordinating event registration activities and maintaining event or ticketing databases (e.g., 4Waves, Eventbrite) Experience coordinating meetings, including schedules, agendas, materials, action and follow-up items Experience supporting event-related financial administration, including cost estimates, purchases or procurement, and expense reimbursements (e.g., Concur) Demonstrated proficiency with MS Office and other relevant administrative, collaboration and content-development tools and platforms (e.g., SharePoint, Planner, Airtable, Canva, AI-enabled productivity tools) Advanced written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with a wide variety of internal and external contacts Excellent organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines Strong problem-solving skills and sound judgment, with the ability to resolve event-related issues and escalate as appropriate Assets (Nonessential): Knowledge of the Temerty Faculty of Medicine Knowledge of the infectious disease research and innovation landscape within the University of Toronto and affiliated health institutions To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Closing Date: 09/22/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Grant - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 09 --  $67,916. with an annual step progression to a maximum of  $86,855. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Hospitality Recruiter: Sana J Mahmood Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Rehabilitation, Event Planning, EMR, Equity, Healthcare, Hospitality, Research, Finance Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
