University College Department: College Administration Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00054197 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Faculty of Arts & Science is the heart of Canada’s leading university and one of the most comprehensive and diverse academic divisions in the world. The strength of Arts & Science derives from our combined teaching and research excellence in the humanities, sciences and social sciences across 29 departments, seven colleges and 46 interdisciplinary centres, institutes and programs. We can only realize our mission with the dedication and excellence of engaged staff and faculty. The diversity of opportunities and perspectives within the Faculty reflect the local and global landscape and the need for curiosity, innovative thinking and collaboration. At Arts & Science, we take pride in our legacy of innovation and discovery that has changed the way we think about the world. Your opportunity: Reporting to the Chief Administrative Officer, the Finance and Payroll Assistant supports University College's Operating and Trust portfolio . The incumbent provides financial administrative and reporting support through budget monitoring, account reconciliation, preparation of budget variance information, comparison of forecasted figures to actuals, and the processing of payroll and other financial transactions. Working within established University policies and procedures, the incumbent identifies and resolves discrepancies, verifies the accuracy and completeness of financial information, and supports the Financial Officer by gathering information required for budget planning and reporting across multiple operating and trust accounts. Your responsibilities will include: Reconciling accounts Monitoring department budget to ensure expenditure remains within budgeted allocations Monitoring, recording, reconciling and/or reporting on trust accounts Identifying and resolving individual financial discrepancies Preparing budget variance reports Gathering information in preparation for budget planning Comparing forecasted figures to actuals Processing payroll Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or acceptable combination of equivalent experience. Minimum three (3) years of relevant experience in financial administration, accounting and/or payroll in a complex institutional or multi-account environment. Experience monitoring and reconciling operating, trust or comparable restrictive accounts and identifying and resolving financial discrepancies. Experience monitoring budgets, preparing budget variance information, and gathering financial information to support budget planning and forecasting processes. Experience processing payroll, reconciling payroll distributions, and resolving payroll and/or HRIS processing issues. Experience with accounts payable/receivable, journal entries, cost recoveries, purchasing card reconciliation and expense reimbursement processes. Experience working with Financial Information Systems (FIS) and Human Resources Information Systems (HRIS) or equivalent systems Sound knowledge of generally accepted accounting principles and financial controls. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Office, particularly Excel, and demonstrated ability to work accurately with financial data. Ability to manage competing deadlines in a fast-paced environment with initiative, flexibility and strong attention to detail. Strong organizational, problem-solving, verbal and written communication skills, with demonstrated ability to provide responsive client service. Assets (Non-essential) Familiarity with payroll processing for USW Casuals, CUPE Unit 1, Unit 3 and Unit 5. Familiarity with University of Toronto financial systems and processes, including Concur and UTime. Experience working with multiple funds, cost centres or comparable financial structures is strongly preferred. To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Courteous Efficient Meticulous Multi-tasker Organized Problem solver Responsible Closing Date: 09/22/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 09 --  $67,916. with an annual step progression to a maximum of  $86,855. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Finance/Budget/Planning/Audit Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Payroll, Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, Equity, Financial, Finance Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Advancement-Operations-Officer-ON/606013817/": {
      "title": "Advancement Operations Officer Job Details",
      "description": "Advancement Operations Officer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Advancement Operations Officer Date Posted: 09/11/2026 Req ID: 50144 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering Department: FASE: Advancement Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00019918 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Office of Advancement seeks to sustain and enhance the University’s academic mission, leadership, and worldwide impact, by engaging alumni and private-sector stakeholders in the mission of the University. We seek to build mutually beneficial relationships of increasing value and satisfaction over time while seizing new opportunities to strengthen our role in civic and global society, provide a transformational undergraduate learning experience, pave the way for game-changing startups and new industries, drive breakthroughs in health care, and create the knowledge that illuminates humanity. Together, we reimagine the world. Your opportunity: As the Advancement Operations Officer, you will play a pivotal role in supporting fundraising, donor engagement, and alumni relations initiatives within the Faculty of Applied Science & Engineering. This highly collaborative position serves as the operational backbone of the advancement team, supporting prospect and stewardship activities, managing critical data and records, supporting senior staff, and supporting the seamless execution of donor relations and alumni events and priorities. The incumbent will also support the team with invoice and expense processing and other administrative tasks. The ideal candidate is an organized, detail-oriented professional who enjoys building positive relationships, and is passionate about helping advance the faculty's philanthropic goals through exceptional administrative, operational, and data management support. Your responsibilities will include: Responding to inquiries from donor and alumni and escalating as necessary Coordinating meeting schedules, agendas, materials, action and follow-up items, and resolves scheduling conflicts Determining logistical details and activities for development activities, including intake of donation cheques, mailing campaigns, conducting outreach calls, and drafting correspondences to donors Performing data management tasks including: data entry, collating and organizing data for reports, updating and maintaining database records, and verifying donor records are coded correctly Performing financial responsibilities by submitting expense reimbursements, verifying invoices, reconciling purchasing card statements and procuring office supplies Arranging accommodations including; booking rooms, audio-visual, catering, couriers Maintaining supply levels for office supplies Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma in a related field, or an acceptable equivalent combination of education and experience Minimum three (3) years of demonstrated experience providing front line administrative support and customer service in a university, not-for-profit, fundraising or similar environment Experience maintaining senior staff calendars, coordinating meeting schedules, agendas, materials, action and follow up items, resolving scheduling conflicts and responding to inquiries from a wide variety of stakeholders Demonstrated experience collating and organizing data for reports, as well as identifying and resolving data anomalies and discrepancies Demonstrated experience fostering positive relationships with internal and external stakeholders Experience submitting expense reimbursements in Concur (or similar expense reimbursement platform) Experience maintaining and updating administrative processes Experience with updating and maintaining Arbor, or similar CRM platform Proficiency with MS Office Suite (Word, Excel, SharePoint) Knowledge of fundraising processes Knowledge of the advancement profession combined with an understanding of the University’s advancement programs Professional demeanor with a strong customer service orientation and effective interpersonal skills Excellent oral and written communication skills. Strong commitment to accuracy and attention to detail Excellent organizational skills, time management and problem-solving skills with the ability to meet conflicting priorities and balance multiple projects Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and the promotion of a respectful and collegial learning and work environment Ability to work independently, show initiative and exercise diplomacy and good judgment, and also the ability to work cooperatively Proven effectiveness in relating to all levels of faculty, staff, students and individuals external to the University Assets (Nonessential): Experience with the University’s financial policies, procedures, and guidelines To be successful in this role you will be: Communicator Goal oriented Intuitive Organized Problem solver Closing Date: 09/21/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 08 --  $63,963. with an annual step progression to a maximum of  $81,797. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Operations Manager, Data Entry, Audio Visual, Administrative Assistant, Engineer, Operations, Administrative, Creative, Engineering Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
