      "description": "Special Projects Officer Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Special Projects Officer Date Posted: 09/10/2026 Req ID: 50143 Faculty/Division: VP-People, Finance & Digital Services Department: Office of the Chief Financial Officer Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Finance Division is responsible for the University's overall financial policies, systems, and controls, within a decentralized financial management structure. The Division provides financial leadership and services to the University, establishing and monitoring financial policies and procedures, ensuring accurate financial controls are in place, setting direction for financial information systems, and producing financial reports and analysis. Your opportunity: Under the general direction of the Manager, Strategic Initiatives, the Special Projects Officer leads the delivery of complex, cross-functional projects from concept through implementation, applying structured project management methodologies to scope, plan, budget, schedule, and manage risk across the full project lifecycle. Operating within an enterprise-wide context, you will ensure projects align with institutional priorities and are delivered on time, on budget, and to a high standard, generating measurable, long-term value for the University. This role requires access to sensitive and confidential information related to workforce planning and organizational design in support of enterprise transformation efforts. Your responsibilities will include: ●    Leading initiatives from concept through to well-defined, approved projects, determining and applying appropriate project management methodologies and securing stakeholder buy-in ●    Leading project teams and, where applicable, external consultants to deliver outcomes within defined scope, time, and budget ●    Developing and managing project budgets and procurement processes, including RFP development and vendor selection, and establishing performance metrics to assess outcomes ●    Applying critical path analysis and scheduling techniques (e.g., Gantt charts, dependency mapping) and estimation techniques to build realistic timelines and cost projections ●    Utilizing project management software to track progress, resources, and deliverables across active initiatives ●    Building and maintaining a risk register, and analyzing and managing project-specific risks and opportunities to enhance efficiency, effectiveness, and value ●    Actively managing change and scope throughout the project lifecycle to ensure stakeholder satisfaction and achievement of objectives ●    Conducting benefit realization tracking post-implementation to confirm that projects delivered their intended value ●    Facilitating implementation planning, documenting decisions and agreements, guiding related policy and procedure development, and addressing barriers to long-term sustainability with internal and external stakeholders ●    Conducting stakeholder assessments to define objectives, scope, priorities, and success measures, supported by cost-benefit, risk, and SWOT analyses ●    Providing strategic and functional advice to senior leaders, and preparing briefings, summaries, and reports for executive decision-making ●    Supporting institutional operational excellence initiatives as required Essential Qualifications: ●    Minimum four (4) years of progressively responsible experience leading or supporting complex, cross-functional projects through the full project lifecycle in a complex, preferably academic or public-sector, environment ●    Proven experience applying structured project management methodologies, including scope definition, integrated planning and scheduling, budgeting, procurement, and risk management ●    Demonstrated experience coordinating multiple stakeholders and workstreams, and supporting governance and decision-making processes to deliver projects within defined time, resource, and quality parameters ●    Experience supporting change management efforts, including assessing impacts, engaging stakeholders, and contributing to the sustainability of new processes or systems ●    University degree required; graduate degree an asset, or an equivalent combination of education and experience ●    Project management qualifications considered an asset ●    Strong analytical and structured problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing timelines, risks, and dependencies ●    Advanced Microsoft Office and project management software skills, along with strong political acuity and sound judgment when handling confidential and sensitive information Assets (Nonessential): ●    Familiarity with Microsoft SharePoint and Microsoft Project ●    Familiarity with Adobe Acrobat and other Adobe software ●    Familiarity with Lucidchart and Azure DevOps (ADO) To be successful in this role you will be: ●    Organized ●    Logical ●    Strategic thinker ●    Analytical ●    Detail-oriented ●    Problem solver ●    Politically astute ●    Collaborative Note: This is a fully onsite, three (3) year term position. Closing Date: 09/24/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Note: This is a fully onsite, three (3) year term position. Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $93,592 - $109,190 -- Broadband Salary Range: $93,592  - $155,985 Job Category: Finance/Budget/Planning/Audit Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Risk Management, Change Management, Project Manager, Procurement, Information Systems, Finance, Management, Technology, Operations Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
