    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Associate-Professor-Microbiologist-in-Chief-ON/605086617/": {
      "title": "Associate/ Professor",
      "description": "Associate/ Professor - Microbiologist-in-Chief Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Associate/ Professor - Microbiologist-in-Chief Date Posted: 08/10/2026 Closing Date: 09/14/2026 , 11:59PM ET Req ID: 49795 Job Category: Faculty - Clinical Faculty/Division: Faculty of Medicine Department: Dept of Lab. Medicine & Pathobiology Hospital Affiliation: Sinai Health System Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: Applications are invited for the Chief of Microbiology and Medical Director at Sinai Health System (SHS), a fully affiliated hospital of the University of Toronto, comprised of Mount Sinai Hospital, Hennick Bridgepoint Hospital, Lunenfeld-Tanenbaum Research Institute and Circle of Care. SHS combines acute care, complex and rehabilitative care, primary care, home care, and other community-based services to create an innovative and integrated continuum of care, meeting the needs of complex patients. We are seeking an experienced, contemporary leader, able to develop and implement a strategic vision, build teams and establish productive partnerships. The Department of Microbiology at Sinai Health has a longstanding commitment to upholding the core Sinai Values of Service, Humanity, Discovery and Inclusivity and seeks a Chief who can present a vision for operational effectiveness, public responsiveness, and academic excellence to sustain and expand the Department’s impact. The successful candidate must be eligible for a full-time clinical academic appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Full Professor at the University of Toronto. Effective start date is December 1, 2026 or shortly thereafter. The Microbiologist-in-Chief and Medical Director is responsible for collaboratively leading the Department in achieving operational and academic goals, including high-quality clinical impact, education, and research. To support the ongoing growth and development of the Microbiology Department, we are seeking a visionary, strategic leader to build on existing strengths, while shaping the future trajectory of the Department. The Chief will work with operational and medical leaders at Sinai Health and the University of Toronto to develop and implement a forward-thinking, renewed strategy for the Department in alignment with Sinai Health’s Strategic Plan – Discovering and Delivering Life Changing Care , the hospital’s Quality Aims and the University’s priorities, reflected in the Sinai Health Research Strategic Plan . The Department Chief will also work with the Sinai Health Foundation to develop and facilitate philanthropic funding. These deliverables are supported through a dyadic leadership structure. The Microbiologist-in-Chief leadership role is positionally associated with the Dr. Donald Low Chair in Infectious Diseases, a Sinai 100 Chair. Established to enable academic growth and impact in the field, the Chair honours Dr. Donald Low's legacy of excellence in research, education, mentorship, and clinical leadership. The successful candidate will articulate a vision for advancing clinical innovation, scholarship, and collaborative research in microbiology and infectious diseases while translating discoveries into improvements in patient care and public health, consistent with the expectations of a Temerty Faculty of Medicine endowed chair. The successful candidate must hold an MD degree and have or be eligible for licensure in Ontario. They should have specialty certification in Medical Microbiology from the Royal College of Physicians and Surgeons of Canada and be eligible for a senior academic appointment (Associate Professor or Full Professor) in the Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology, Temerty Faculty of Medicine at the University of Toronto. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of academic excellence and scholarship consistent with the expectations of a University of Toronto endowed Chair. The successful candidate will be a role model, with superior leadership qualities, strong operational management skills, and demonstrated commitment to mentoring junior faculty and fostering partnerships within the hospital and the broader academic and healthcare community. They will have a demonstrated ability to create and maintain a workplace and learning environment that is respectful, safe for all staff, trainees and patients. Salaried remuneration for leadership and clinical microbiology activities is commensurate with qualifications, trajectory and associated time commitment and exceeds $375,000 per annum. The Microbiologist-in-Chief is expected to continue active medical practice. The position is for a 5-year term, renewable once, based upon a successful review. Applications for this position will be accepted until September 14, 2026. Interested candidates should forward a cover letter that describes their interest in the position, curriculum vitae and names of three referees to: Lesley Wiesenfeld, MD, EVP Academic and Medical Affairs Sinai Health System 600 University Avenue 19-316 Toronto, On M5G 1X5 Medical.Affairs@SinaiHealth.ca CAUTION: This ad is “posted only” to the UofT affiliated hospital job board. Please see the information directly above for the application instructions; applications submitted via the \"Apply Now\" button on this page will NOT be considered for this position. As one of the largest departments of its kind, the Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology (LMP) has more than 450 faculty including basic scientists, pathologists, laboratory physicians and scientists. By combining research with clinical practice, we are uniquely positioned to translate new findings into reality. As a result, we are known as leaders in diagnosing and treating patients and populations, making an impact locally, nationally and internationally. For more information about the Department of Laboratory Medicine and Pathobiology, University of Toronto please visit our website at www.lmp.utoronto.ca . Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Pathology, Rehabilitation, Public Health, Patient Care, Home Care, Healthcare Apply now » Find similar jobs: All Opportunities, Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Assistant%2C-Associate-or-Full-Professor-General-Hematology-Specialist-ON/602645117/": {
