    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Project-Management-&-IT-Network-Specialist-ON/606107917/": {
      "title": "Project Management & IT Network Specialist",
      "description": "Project Management & IT Network Specialist Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Project Management & IT Network Specialist Date Posted: 09/15/2026 Req ID: 49698 Faculty/Division: VP-People, Finance & Digital Services Department: Enterprise Infrastructure Solutions Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00007509 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: The Enterprise Infrastructure Solutions (EIS) group, part of the Information Technology Services (ITS) division, is responsible for campus core network, campus wireless, wide area network connectivity and internet connectivity for the University, including connectivity to research and education networks. EIS is also responsible for services related to departmental network management, network, server and storage infrastructure, Windows and Linux server management services, database and application integration and support, enterprise backup service, 24/7 operation of central administrative data centres and telecommunications services. If you’re motivated and passionate about learning technologies and dedicated to improving experiences for today’s student, consider a career with us. Your opportunity: Reporting to Manager, Network Design and Implementation, the Project Management IT Network Specialist will be part of a highly skilled and collaborative technical team responsible for designing, building, and operating secure, scalable, and cost-efficient data networks for the University. This role is strongly hands-on, with a primary focus on network infrastructure planning, design, engineering, operational reliability, and cost efficiency. You will be working in close partnership with network operations and information security teams, departmental IT leadership, University Planning, Design & Construction, field service technicians, and service delivery team. The role contributes to University departments and services through network infrastructure design, enablement, and support. The position requires strong practicalexpertise in leading and planning IT projects, designing, implementing, and troubleshooting complex IP networks. You will be developing and updating network infrastructure for highly complex and confidential university-wide IT systems. Strong leadership and training skills are required; you will be serving as a resource on specific issues to a group of specialists, also, leading a group of technicians during network implementation and testing phases of projects, including responsibility for scheduling and/or workflow. The ideal candidate has a substantial experience in designing and implementing complex IP-based networks on a campus scale, demonstrated ability to work both independently and in collaboration with peer groups and services. Your responsibilities will include: Planning and implementing expansion and enhancement of IT networks independently Analyzing, testing, troubleshooting highly complex networking systems Devising solutions to operational problems within the capacity and operational limitations of installed equipment Collaborating with peers and senior management on network planning, implementation, and troubleshooting across the campus Creating complex and technical documentation and user support guides Leading and planning IT network projects on the building, system and campus scale. Planning and estimating financial resources required for programs and/or projects. Collaborating on cost estimates. Serving as a resource on specific issues to a group of specialists Essential Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science, Computer Networking, Network Engineering or related field. Equivalent combination of education and experience will be considered. Minimum five years of experience in the design, specification andimplementation of enterprise networks and project management. Proficiency working with a variety of IPEthernet-based communications network hardware (e.g., Aruba CX6000/8000 switches or equivalent models, Aruba Wi-Fi 5/6/7 WAPs or equivalent) related diagnostic and network management tools (e.g., WireShark, Netdisco, ClearPass, Aruba Networking Central, AirWave, Ekahau, or equivalent) and test equipment (OTDR, Ekahau Sidekick, and similar) . Proven track record of working in a team environment and providing team leadership. Demonstrated ability to manage complex networking projects to ensure proper and timely project implementation. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to produce quality project documentation and reports. Comfortable operating in complex project management environments where influence, persuasion, and relationship-building are as important as technical expertise. Assets (Nonessential): Relevant certification in networking (CCNA, CCNP or equivalent, BICSI RCDD, PMP). To be successful in this role you will be: Goal oriented Multi-tasker Problem solver Team player Closing Date: 09/28/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 16 --  $103,367. with an annual step progression to a maximum of  $132,188. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Information Technology (IT) Recruiter: Khristen Sivaramalingam Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Project Manager, Design Engineer, Network, Network Engineer, Telecom, Technology, Engineering Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
