    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Education-Assistant-ON/606122917/": {
      "title": "Education Assistant",
      "description": "Education Assistant Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Education Assistant Date Posted: 09/15/2026 Req ID: 50187 Faculty/Division: Temerty Faculty of Medicine Department: Department of Psychiatry Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Position Number: 00059796 Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Home to over 40 departments and institutes, the University of Toronto's Temerty Faculty of Medicine lies at the heart of the Toronto Academic Health Science Network and is a global leader in ground-breaking research and education, spanning clinical medicine, basic science and the rehabilitation sciences sectors. Your opportunity: As one of the largest Departments of Psychiatry in the world, we serve as a catalyst for progress, mobilizing partners and resources to improve the outcome of those living with mental illness. We strive to provide the best care to today’s patients and to transform the understanding and treatment of mental illness and addiction for the patients of tomorrow. As the Education Assistant, you will play an integral role in supporting education programs within the Department of Psychiatry’s growing education portfolio, including the three subspecialty programs, fellowships, and related faculty development initiatives. You will coordinate a wide variety of program tasks that require strong attention to detail and adaptability within a fast-paced environment. Through excellent organizational and communication skills, you will contribute to the effective coordination and delivery of the Department’s educational activities. Your responsibilities will include: Providing detailed information to learners on program requirements, supporting learner needs, and tracking and monitoring learner progress Acting as the first point of contact for general enquiries, and responding within the defined scope of the role Liaising with learners, faculty, and internal and external contacts to coordinate program activities, seminars, and workshops Coordinating meeting schedules, agendas, materials, action and follow-up items, and taking and distributing meeting minutes Supporting internal and external program reviews by coordinating required materials and documentation Determining logistical details and activities for events and/or programming Handling sensitive and/or confidential information, updating and maintaining records, and generating reports Essential Qualifications: Advanced College Diploma (3 years) or an acceptable combination of education and experience Minimum two (2) years of experience supporting and coordinating education programs and projects Demonstrated experience providing frontline learner support, including serving as a first point of contact for enquiries and providing program information Demonstrated experience tracking and monitoring learners and checking completion of program requirements Demonstrated experience coordinating meetings, including schedules, agendas, materials, action and follow-up items, and taking meeting minutes Experience organizing and executing events both in person and virtually, including coordinating logistics Experience maintaining information in databases and digital platforms, updating program records, and generating reports Strong proficiency with MS Office and other common administrative tools and systems (e.g., shared mailboxes and calendars, Zoom) Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to liaise effectively with learners, faculty, and internal and external contacts Excellent organizational and time-management skills, with demonstrated ability to prioritize activities and meet deadlines Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion, professionalism, and sound judgment To be successful in thisrole you will be: Communicator Multi-tasker Organized Tactful Closing Date: 09/23/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: USW Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: USW Pay Band 08 --  $63,963. with an annual step progression to a maximum of  $81,797. Pay scale and job class assignment is subject to determination pursuant to the Job Evaluation/Pay Equity Maintenance Protocol. Job Category: Student Services Recruiter: Sana J Mahmood Lived Experience Statement Candidates who are members of Indigenous, Black, racialized and 2SLGBTQ+ communities, persons with disabilities, and other equity deserving groups are encouraged to apply, and their lived experience shall be taken into consideration as applicable to the posted position. Job descriptions are available upon request for internal applicants. Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Rehabilitation, Behavioral Health, Substance Abuse, Education, Healthcare, Research Apply now » Find similar jobs: USW Staff Appointed Opportunities, Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
