    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Strategic-Engagement-&-Experience-Design-Lead-ON/606096317/": {
      "title": "Strategic Engagement & Experience Design Lead Job Details",
      "description": "Strategic Engagement & Experience Design Lead Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Strategic Engagement & Experience Design Lead Date Posted: 09/14/2026 Req ID: 50167 Faculty/Division: Rotman School of Management Department: Joseph L. Rotman School of Management Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: The Rotman School of Management is part of the University of Toronto, a global centre of research and academic excellence at the heart of Canada’s commercial and financial capital. Rotman is a catalyst for transformative learning, insights and public engagement, bringing together diverse views and initiatives around a defining purpose: to create value for business and society. We make a fundamental promise - Here’s where it changes - to our students, our partners and the broader community. Everyone at Rotman, faculty and staff, plays a role in bringing that promise to life. Business Design is Rotman’s approach to learning and acting in innovative ways using human-centered design methods. It allows current and future leaders to learn about what both customers need and stakeholders want. Rotman’s Business Design Initiative (BDI) encompasses all design-related education and community engagement activities. BDI’s mission is to integrate business design into the business school curriculum in order to position Rotman as a leader in business design education and to increase the competitiveness of our students seeking industry roles. Reporting to the Academic Director of the Business Design Initiative (BDI), the Strategic Engagement and Experience Design Lead is responsible for leading Student Engagement and BDI’s Community of Practice. The incumbent is accountable for all administrative functions related to the BDI and its performance including management of the Administrative & Communications Assistant, budgets and planning, and is the primary contact for all matters relating to the BDI. The Strategic Engagement and Experience Design Lead will work to understand the needs of BDI’s student stakeholders and will collaborate with the Academic Director to design programs that elevate their experience at Rotman and create meaningful connections with industry partners. They will also keep a pulse on shifts in the business design space in industry and develop programs that continue to position Rotman/BDI as a thought leader in business design and human centered innovation. The role is involved with all co-curricular program design, development and management. The Strategic Engagement and Experience Design Lead will be participating in advisory boards and committees.  The incumbent must develop and maintain strong and productive relationships across varied constituent groups both internally at Rotman and at other faculties. QUALIFICATIONS EDUCATION: An MBA with a focus on human-centered design is required or an equivalent combination of education and experience. A deep understanding of a range of design methodologies for business innovation and human-centered design and familiarity with Rotman’s Business Design methodology is an asset. EXPERIENCE: A minimum of 5 years of industry related experience in business design or related fields such as service design or customer experience (CX). Candidates must have worked directly with senior management across multiple stakeholders and can demonstrate experience in developing strong partnerships and alliances, relationship management, contract negotiations/development. Experience with managing employees. SKILLS: Superior interpersonal and communication skills are required to manage BDI’s relationships with highly diverse and demanding community of both internal (including students, faculty, university administrators, staff and alumni) and external (corporate partners, other academic institutions, professional associations) stakeholders. Strong financial management skills including budget preparation, variance analysis and cost reconciliations. Strong negotiations, critical thinking, political acumen, persuasion and contract development skills OTHER: Ability to demonstrate maturity, professionalism and empathy, and be able to adjust their engagement style to meet stakeholders’ needs. Strong strategic leadership with the ability to define vision and priorities, governance structures, organizational design and resource plans. Independent decision-making, problem finding and creative problem solving. Entrepreneurial leadership with the ability to create and execute new initiatives. Self-motivated and confident with sound judgement and keen diplomatic skills. NOTE: This is a term position ending June 2028. Closing Date: 09/22/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Appointment Type : Budget - Term Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 3 -- Hiring Zone: $93,592 - $109,190 -- Broadband Salary Range: $93,592  - $155,985 Job Category: Administrative / Managerial Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Relationship Manager, MBA, Curriculum, Customer Service, Management, Education, Research, Strategy Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
