      "description": "Cafeteria Worker - Casual (15 Vacancies) Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Cafeteria Worker - Casual (15 Vacancies) Date Posted: 09/17/2026 Req ID: 50235 Faculty/Division: Spaces & Experiences Department: Food Services Campus: St. George (Downtown Toronto) Description: Under general supervision, assembles, prepares and serves food and beverage products and maintains cleanliness of the cafeteria area. May operates a cash register, receive and issue cash. Typical Duties The following illustrative tasks indicate the level of skill required and the extent of the responsibility involved in this position.  They in no way limit the incumbent to the tasks indicated. Flexibility of the employee to perform a wide variety of functions is necessary in successfully fulfilling the requirements of this position.  The degree to which each employee performs each of the following tasks listed below will vary according to where and when the employee is scheduled to work. (a)    assembles work station with appropriate products and equipment; (b)    assembles, prepares, and serves food and beverage products; (c)    cooks stir fry and grill display cooking, may cook some other items; (d)    prepares sandwiches, salads and bakes premixed food products; (e)    advises and provides information to customers such as ingredients, pricing, portion size; (f)    collects dishes and tableware used by customers and places them in appropriate areas for washing; (g)    cleans table tops, counters and furniture in cafeteria and surrounding area; (h)    maintains adequate supplies of dishes, utensils and food and paper products in various receptacles for use by customers; (i)    removes soiled tableware and garbage to specific locations, sorts recyclable materials; (j)    scrubs pots and pans; and washes dishes (k)     cleans floors; staff locker rooms and washrooms; (l)    receives and stores food and supplies; checks receiving slips for accuracy; (m)    sets up and prepares cash register, receives cash float and sets up cash appropriately; keys menu prices into cash register if required. (n)     prepares reports at the end of each shift; (o)     writes special menus and their prices on menu board; (p)    prepares condiment and dessert counters; (q)     balances cash at the end of the shift, delivers cash to accountant or locks in safe; (r)     may keep records of stores on hand; and (s)    other related duties as required. Minimum Requirements for Selection Education:    Completion of Grade 12 or equivalent. Experience:    One year of related working experience. Other:    Physical ability to perform required duties, ability to communicate effectively in English (oral and written), considerable public relations skills (courtesy and tact) and may be required to complete a University of Toronto server training program. Knowledge of food safety. Ability to work well in a team setting. Ability to handle figures rapidly. Closing Date: 09/26/2026, 11:59PM ET Employee Group: Hourly, CUPE 3261 Casual Appointment Type : Casual Part-Time Schedule: Flexible schedule required, which may include morning, evening and weekend hours Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: $25.96 per hour Job Category: Facilities/Ancillary Services Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: Cashier, Food Safety, PR, Accounting, Part Time, Hospitality, Marketing, Quality, Finance Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
    },
    "https://jobs.utoronto.ca/job/Toronto-Director%2C-Finance-&-Procurement-ON/606202717/": {
      "title": "Director, Finance & Procurement",
      "description": "Director, Finance & Procurement Job Details | University of Toronto Skip to main content Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities Faculty Opportunities Librarian Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Sign in as Casual / External / View Profile U of T Employee Sign In Home Current Opportunities All Opportunities Staff Opportunities USW Staff Appointed Opportunities Faculty Opportunities UTemp (Short-Term) Affiliated Hospital Opportunities Librarian Opportunities Student Opportunities Federated Colleges Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Opportunities CUPE 3902 (Unit 3) Emergency Posting Opportunities Applying to U of T Frequently Asked Questions Working at U of T People, Finance & Digital Services Workplace Inclusion Join Our Talent Network Search Keywords More Filter Options: Campus and Job Category Loading... Campus All Job Category All Clear Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Create Alert × Select how often (in days) to receive an alert: Apply now » Director, Finance & Procurement Date Posted: 09/17/2026 Req ID: 50223 Faculty/Division: Faculty of Dentistry Department: Faculty of Dentistry Campus : St. George (Downtown Toronto) Existing Vacancy: Yes Description: About us: Exciting new advances and global challenges are radically reshaping the field of dentistry. Our vision at the Faculty of Dentistry at the University of Toronto is to not just address and respond to these changes – but to thoughtfully and conscientiously shape the field of the future.With our robust and comprehensive educational training programs (DDS, MSc, PhD degrees, IDAPP and other specialty programs), our emphasis on community outreach and care, and our internationally known and interdisciplinary research mission, the Faculty of Dentistry at the University of Toronto continues to earn its reputation as one of the top dental schools in North America. Throughout more than 150 years of dental education -- the oldest, largest and most comprehensive training program in Canada -- we have striven to graduate the highest quality of students while providing the public the highest standards of care. We are driven by our vision to improve health by advancing dentistry through inspired leadership, innovation, and excellence in education, research and practice. Your Opportunity: Working independently under the general direction of the Chief Administrative Officer (CAO), the Director, Finance and Procurement provides strategic leadership, counsel/advise, expertise and integrity in the planning, management and administration of all financial resources and procurement activities for the Faculty of  Dentistry. The Director, Finance and Procurement has a broad and complex set of responsibilities to ensure the Faculty’s financial and procurement goals, objectives and priorities are met; and, in ensuring that the resource implications of these activities for the academic, research, Continuing Dental Education (CDE) and clinic operations are identified and addressed. The incumbent is responsible for the planning and development of the Faculty of Dentistry’s annual budgets (academic, research, CDE and dental clinics). Under the direction of the CAO, the incumbent plans and develops short and long‐term academic budget planning and modelling. The Director of Finance and Procurement ensures the dental clinics financial matters align with the overall Faculty’s strategic budget model and academic plan as it relates to the dental clinics. The incumbent oversees and administers the annual budget process for ancillary fees, including procurement of hundreds of items for undergraduate, graduate and non-degree programs. The incumbent works closely with the CAO, Director of Clinical Affairs, Associate Director of Clinical Operations and clinic staff to ensure that clinic revenues are maximized and expenditures are controlled. The incumbent is also responsible for planning and implementing strategic procurement including sourcing strategy, supplier selection and evaluation, quality management, customer relationship management and performance assessment along with the oversight of the Faculty’s e‐commerce and clinic patient registration system from a financial perspective. The Director is responsible for delivering data that support key priorities of the Faculty. The incumbent oversees the use of data, reporting and analytics products that generate insights for the Faculty. Qualifications Required: EDUCATION: University degree (Master's level preferred) in business/commerce/accounting/ with a recognized professional accounting designation such as CMA, CGA, CPA or an equivalent combination of education and experience. EXPERIENCE: Minimum of 5 years related experience in University administration or the public sector. Experience with UofT and a strong knowledge of University financial and procurement policies and procedures is preferred. Experience in large public sector or clinical environment an asset. Ability to effectively communicate technical accounting principles to non‐accounting people, ideas and information in written and oral format to Faculty leadership, administrative staff, faculty members and students. Demonstrated expertise in budget planning, financial management and control, as well as administration of budget and resources. Experience with strategic planning, scenario analysis, forecasting and experience working in a team environment across diverse constituents and stakeholders. Extensive contract management experience. Experience in the application of sound financial principles and practices. Experience in effectively communicating financial information to departmental administrators. Proven experience in Human Resources Management, preferably in a unionized environment. SKILLS: Excellent financial management, organizational and analytical skills. Excellent communication skills. Strong leadership. Strong problem solving and decision‐making skills. Demonstrated superior planning, budgeting and project management skills. Strong computer skills with advanced proficiency in Microsoft Word and Excel. Experience with FIS, HRIS, and AMS platforms and other reporting platforms. SAP knowledge an asset. Effective negotiator with superior interpersonal and multi‐tasking skills. OTHER: Proven ability to think strategically, build effective teams and work effectively with people at all levels of the organization, work independently as well as part of a team, and ability to be self‐directed and take initiative. A collaborative and consultative management style as well as the ability to foster and maintain effective relationships. Ability to understand and solve complex problems, often under pressure, requiring extensive follow‐ up with both internal and external constituencies. Ability to analyze and understand problems from multiple perspectives, in order to understand the impact on multiple areas and determine the optimal solution. Ability to balance different opinions and perspectives and find solutions in a positive, consensus‐ building manner. Keen attention to detail and accuracy. Proven ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise discretion, tact, and good judgment at all times. Knowledgeable in the areas of equity, diversity, and inclusion as it relates to daily operations and Faculty initiatives. Proven ability to deal with a variety of tasks and meet strict deadlines. Ability to frequently adjust priorities. Closing Date: 09/30/2026,11:59PM ET Employee Group: Salaried Personnel Subarea: PM Appointment Type : Budget - Continuing Schedule: Full-Time Pay Scale Group & Hiring Zone: PM 5 -- Hiring Zone: $120,499 - $140,583 -- Broadband Salary Range: $120,499 - $200,831 Job Category: Finance/Budget/Planning/Audit Diversity Statement The University of Toronto embraces Diversity and is building a culture of belonging that increases our capacity to effectively address and serve the interests of our global community. We strongly encourage applications from Indigenous Peoples, Black and racialized persons, women, persons with disabilities, and people of diverse sexual and gender identities. We value applicants who have demonstrated a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and recognize that diverse perspectives, experiences, and expertise are essential to strengthening our academic mission. As part of your application, you will be asked to complete a brief Diversity Survey. This survey is voluntary. Any information directly related to you is confidential and cannot be accessed by search committees or human resources staff. Results will be aggregated for institutional planning purposes. For more information, please see http://uoft.me/UP . Accessibility Statement The University strives to be an equitable and inclusive community, and proactively seeks to increase diversity among its community members. Our values regarding equity and diversity are linked with our unwavering commitment to excellence in the pursuit of our academic mission. The University is committed to the principles of the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). As such, we strive to make our recruitment, assessment and selection processes as accessible as possible and provide accommodations as required for applicants with disabilities. If you require any accommodations at any point during the application and hiring process, please contact uoft.careers@utoronto.ca . Job Segment: CRM, Procurement, Quality Manager, Relationship Manager, Contract Manager, Technology, Operations, Customer Service, Legal, Quality Apply now » Find similar jobs: Staff Opportunities, All Opportunities Home Accessibility Land Acknowledgment utoronto.ca Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. People, Finance & Digital Services"
